Found by OCP (kubernetes-ocp k246, 2026-10-31) against Hetzner's OpenAPI spec (docs.hetzner.cloud/cloud.spec.json) and the changelog entry of Oct 08: "Field deprecated will be removed".

- **The field name is wrong.** The POD of WWW::Hetzner::Cloud::ServerType says each `locations` entry has a `deprecated` field. Per the spec, each entry has `id`, `name`, `deprecation` (an object or null), `recommended` and `available`. There is no `deprecated` key. The library passes the data through unchanged, so code that follows the docs and filters on `{deprecated}` hides nothing.
- **The top-level field goes away.** Hetzner removes the top-level `deprecated` response field from Server Types, Images and Load Balancer Types on **2 November 2026**. The replacement for server types is the per-location `deprecation`; for images and LB types it is the top-level `deprecation`.
- **The consumer skill has the same error.** perl-www-hetzner (sourced from this repo) shows `!$_->{deprecated}` as its example and says "Test the per-location deprecated". Both need to say `deprecation`.

Done when:
- the POD lists the real per-location keys;
- the `->deprecated` accessors on ServerType, Image and LoadBalancerType are documented as gone after 2026-11-02, or are removed or derived from `deprecation`, whichever the maintainer prefers;
- the consumer skill example uses `deprecation`;
- a test with a fixture shaped like the spec pins the per-location keys.

